# Line endings for files that are *executed by Linux*, not merely read there.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, which
# rewrites text files to CRLF on checkout. For most of the tree that is
# harmless. For anything with a shebang it is not: bash reads the first line of
# a CRLF script as `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`, fails to find an interpreter by that
# name, and reports "bad interpreter" naming a file that plainly exists.
#
# The trap is that it does not bite the machine that committed the file -- the
# working copy is whatever it was written as -- only a *fresh clone*. So it
# survives every local test and fails for the next person.
#
# Not hypothetical here: the AppImage build runs `packaging/linux/*.sh` inside
# WSL, and the server's systemd units and BlueZ snippets are parsed by daemons
# that treat a trailing \r as part of the value.

* text=auto

# Shell scripts: executed by bash, in WSL and on the Pi.
*.sh            text eol=lf

# systemd units and drop-ins: a trailing \r lands inside ExecStart.
*.service       text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.snippet       text eol=lf

# The broker's container: the Dockerfile's RUN lines and the healthcheck run
# inside Linux, and the compose file is parsed there too.
packaging/docker/Dockerfile      text eol=lf
packaging/docker/*.py            text eol=lf
packaging/docker/*.yml           text eol=lf

# frp reads these on the VPS and on the Pi.
packaging/frp/*.toml             text eol=lf

# Generated art and icons are binary; never let a newline rule near them.
*.png           binary
*.ico           binary
*.AppImage      binary
